<!-- ======================================================================
     EFV_Text.xml  (modinfo InGameActions UpdateText EFV_Text)
     Owner: WP1.6 (complete key set for all phases; later phases may reword).
     Format (PLAN 4.2, R4 7): <Row Tag="LOC_EFV_..." Language="en_US">.
     Plurals: {1_Num : plural 1?turn; other?turns;} (base-game syntax).

     NOT here: LOC_EFV_MOD_TITLE / _TEASER / _DESCRIPTION live in the
     EFV.modinfo <LocalizedText> block (INTERFACES note 10).

     ARGUMENT ORDER (Locale.Lookup(key, a1, a2, ...)). Names are strings
     already localized by the caller; N values are numbers.

     Notifications (EFV_Notify.Queue args array; the SAME array is used for
     _MESSAGE and _SUMMARY; _MESSAGE headlines take no arguments).
     Order = order of first appearance in the spec 14.3 text:
       DEPARTED         1 Unit, 2 City (destination), 3 N transit turns
       ARRIVED          1 Unit, 2 Sender civ, 3 City
       SPAWN_BLOCKED    1 Unit, 2 City
       EXPIRY_SOON      1 Unit, 2 N turns left, 3 Sender civ
       GRACE            1 Unit, 2 Sender civ, 3 N grace turns left
       MUTINY           1 Unit, 2 N turns until destroyed, 3 Sender civ
       MUTINY_DEATH     1 Unit
         D9 alert types (Phase 2): the texts above go to the RECIPIENT (the
         unit's owner). The SENDER gets LOC_<type>_SENDER_MESSAGE / _SUMMARY
         (EXPIRY_SOON, GRACE, MUTINY) with the same argument order, but the
         civ argument is the RECIPIENT civ. Lapsed Volunteers (owned by the
         sender, Phase 3) get only the _SENDER texts.
       RETURNING        1 Unit, 2 City (return city), 3 N transit turns
       RETURNED         1 Unit, 2 City
       REROUTED         1 City (lost), 2 Unit, 3 NewCity
       VOLUNTEER_LAPSE  1 Recipient civ, 2 N grace turns
       ENTRUSTED        1 Capturer civ, 2 City, 3 Recipient civ
       ACCESS_LAPSE     1 Recipient civ, 2 N grace turns          (added)
       UNIT_LOST        1 Unit, 2 loss text = Locale.Lookup(LOC_EFV_LOSS_*) (added)
       MERGED           1 Unit (base text); variants _SURVIVOR / _ABSORBED /
                        _VOLUNTEER: 1 Unit, 2 Sender civ, 3 Recipient civ (Phase 5)
       REVERTED         1 Unit, 2 Sender civ, 3 Recipient civ      (added)
       REQUEST_FAILED   1 reason text = Locale.Lookup(LOC_EFV_REASON_<code>, ...) (added)
       LAPSE_CANCELLED  1 Recipient civ, 2 Unit                    (added)
       LAPSE_PAUSED     1 Unit, 2 Recipient civ, 3 State text = Locale.Lookup(
                        LOC_EFV_STATE_GRACE / _MUTINY, N) (added 0.5.1, note 29)
       GRACE / MUTINY _VOLUNTEER variants (lapsed Volunteers, 0.5.1): the
                        _SENDER argument order (civ = the recipient)
     (Matches EFV_Transit.lua / EFV_Lifecycle.lua as of WP1.4; the types
     not yet implemented follow the same rule.)
     Other keys (matching the UI call sites in UI/*.lua):
       LOC_EFV_REASON_GOLD              1 fee (UI also passes 2 = gold balance, unused)
       LOC_EFV_REASON_FEE_CHANGED       1 new fee
       LOC_EFV_REASON_RECALL_MIN_TURNS  1 N turns until recall is allowed
       LOC_EFV_REASON_NOT_PARTNER, _VOL_NEEDS_ACCESS, _CS_NOT_MET,
         _AT_WAR_WITH_RECIPIENT, _NO_COMMON_WAR
                                        1 recipient name(s) (EFV_UIShared
                                          NAME_REASON_LIST; comma-joined list
                                          in the Send-button summary)
       LOC_EFV_STATE_*                  1 N (turns; see each row); _BLOCKED,
                                          _DEPLOYED_EXPIRED, _DEPLOYED_VOLUNTEER_READY
                                          take none
       LOC_EFV_LAPSE_WAR / _PARTNER     none (appended to the state text)
       LOC_EFV_STATE_GRACE_PAUSED / _MUTINY_PAUSED
                                        1 N (grace turns left / turns until
                                          destroyed once the mutiny resumes)
       LOC_EFV_DURATION_TURNS           1 N
       LOC_EFV_FEE_GOLD                 1 fee (> 0); LOC_EFV_FEE_FREE none
                                        (EFV_UI_FeeText, 0.5.2: a fee of 0)
       LOC_EFV_CONFIRM_SEND             1 Unit, 2 City, 3 Recipient civ, 4 Fee
                                        text (EFV_UI_FeeText: "Free" or
                                        "N [ICON_Gold] Gold"),
                                        5 Transit turns, 6 Duration text,
                                        7 Force label (EFV_DestinationPicker.lua)
       LOC_EFV_CONFIRM_RECALL           1 Unit
       LOC_EFV_ENTRUST_TO               1 Recipient civ
       LOC_EFV_ENTRUST_TO_TT            1 City, 2 Recipient civ
       LOC_EFV_ENTRUST_CONFIRM          1 City, 2 Recipient civ (armed row tooltip)
       LOC_EFV_ENTRUST_CONFIRM_BUTTON   1 Recipient civ (two-click confirm, PLAN 3.4)
       LOC_EFV_ENTRUST_TT_RECIPIENTS    1 comma list of recipient civs
       LOC_EFV_ENTRUST_NOT_AT_WAR       1 comma list of partner civs, 2 former owner civ
       LOC_EFV_REASON_ENTRUST_NO_PARTNER 1 former owner civ
       LOC_EFV_BANNER_ALERT             1 N units in grace or mutiny, 2 M in mutiny
       LOC_EFV_BANNER_TT_LINE           1 Unit, 2 State text (EFV_UI_StateText)
       LOC_EFV_FLAG_TT                  1 Force label, 2 Unit, 3 Sender civ,
                                        4 Recipient civ, 5 State text
                                        (EFV_UI_StatusTooltip)
       LOC_EFV_WARN_NO_HEAL             1 owner civ, 2 resource (icon + name) (0.6.0)
       LOC_EFV_PLAYER_GENERIC           none (G passes the player ID, UI passes
                                          nothing; the text ignores it)
     Action tooltips: the UI shows Lookup(key) .. [NEWLINE] .. Lookup(key_TT),
     so the _TT texts do not repeat the action name.
     All other keys take no arguments.
     ====================================================================== -->
